---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<Layout title="Beta terms | cppMax" description="Preliminary terms for the cppMax private beta and website.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Beta terms" title="Pre-release software needs clear expectations." description="These draft terms cover the private beta and this website. Final App Store terms will replace or expand them before release." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell policy-layout">
    <aside><strong>Draft terms</strong><span>Updated August 29, 2026</span><p>These are not the final App Store terms.</p></aside>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Beta status</h2><p>cppMax is pre-release software. A feature may change, break, or disappear before the public release. Keep a separate backup of important projects.</p>
      <h2>Your projects</h2><p>You keep ownership of the code and files you create or import. You are responsible for permission to use third-party code, libraries, and repositories.</p>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2><p>Do not use cppMax or its related services to break applicable law, access systems without permission, distribute malware, or infringe somebody else's rights.</p>
      <h2>Pricing statements</h2><p>Automatic signing is free during beta. The stated €3.99 post-beta price, envToken costs, ad option, and prepaid option describe the current plan. They may change before release and do not form a purchase offer today.</p>
      <h2>Availability</h2><p>The beta is provided for testing. Access and uptime are not guaranteed. Do not use the beta as the only copy of critical work or in a safety-critical system.</p>
      <h2>Third-party software</h2><p>cppMax includes open-source development tools and can connect to third-party services. Their licenses and terms continue to apply.</p>
      <h2>Final terms still needed</h2><p>Before public release, these terms need the legal identity of the app operator, governing law, contact details, warranty language, liability terms, termination rules, and App Store provisions.</p>
      <h2>Questions</h2><p>The current contact status is listed on the <a class="text-link" href="/support/">support page</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .policy-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 250px 1fr; gap: 90px; align-items: start; }
  .policy-layout aside { position: sticky; top: 105px; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .policy-layout aside strong, .policy-layout aside span { display: block; }
  .policy-layout aside strong { margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--orange); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .policy-layout aside span { font-weight: 750; }
  .policy-layout aside p { margin: 24px 0 0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .policy-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 45px; } .policy-layout aside { position: static; } }
</style>
